<title>FRANCE: French had 2.73 million mobile phones in February.</title>
<headline>French had 2.73 million mobile phones in February.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of mobile phones in France increased by 4.8 percent in February to 2,726,100, the telecommunications regulator ART said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the digital market, comprising 2.53 million phones, France Telecom's Itineris was the leader with 1.46 million, followed by Generale des Eaux's SFR with 925,400 and Bouygues Telecom with 108,300. There were 197,200 analogue phones.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
